.TH AURAPASS-DESKTOP 1 "2026" "aurapass 1.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aurapass-desktop \- the AuraPass graphical application
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aurapass-desktop
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aurapass-desktop
is the AuraPass desktop application. It opens a vault, unlocks it with the
master password, and lets you browse, edit, generate and audit credentials.
It also hosts the browser bridge in-process, so the extensions work while the
window is open.
.PP
The user interface is built with the
.B iced
toolkit on top of its
.B tiny-skia
software renderer, so it draws its own widgets on the CPU. The only system
services it needs are a Wayland or X11 window and a clipboard: there is no
GPU, EGL or OpenGL requirement, and no graphics driver is loaded.
.SH TRAY ICON AND QUICK ASSISTANT
When a
.B StatusNotifierWatcher
is present on the session bus (Ubuntu, GNOME with the AppIndicator extension,
KDE), AuraPass shows a tray icon with a menu offering
.IR "Open AuraPass" ,
.IR "Quick assistant" ,
.IR "Lock vault"
and
.IR "Quit" .
Left-clicking the icon shows or hides the window; middle-clicking it opens the
quick assistant.
.PP
Closing the window hides it to the tray instead of quitting. Use
.I "Quit"
from the tray menu, or from the menu bar inside the application, to exit.
Both behaviours can be switched off in Settings.
.PP
The quick assistant is a compact, always-on-top panel with the password
generator: password, passphrase and PIN modes, an entropy estimate, and a
history that is held in memory for the session only and never written to
disk. It is usable while the vault is locked, because the generator needs no
vault. It folds away as soon as you click elsewhere. When the main window is
already open the same generator opens inside it as a dialog instead.
.PP
If no
.B StatusNotifierWatcher
is available, AuraPass reports that the tray could not be registered and
closes normally instead of hiding, so the window cannot be lost.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-vault " " \fIFILE\fR
Vault file to open on start.
.TP
.BR \-\-config-dir " " \fIDIR\fR
Use an alternative configuration directory.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/aurapass/config.json
Settings, recent vaults and the browser-bridge pairing token.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AURAPASS_CONFIG_DIR
Override the configuration directory.
.TP
.B AURAPASS_VAULT
Default vault path.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aurapass (1),
.BR aurapass-bridge (1),
.BR aurapass-native-host (1)
